From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Pawe=C5=82=20Phan?= <szop.hektar_1w@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] inittab: start a program without a terminal again too
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An inittab entry whose id names no terminal, "::respawn:/sbin/syslogd",
runs with /dev/null for its input and output. When it ends, procd starts
it again only if its terminal still exists, and for an empty id it looks
for /dev/ itself, which open() does not take: such a program ran once
and never again. OpenWrt's inittab has only the console's entries, so
nothing there showed it.

The terminal is now looked for only when the entry names one.

Upstream: not submitted
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Paweł Phan <szop.hektar_1w@icloud.com>
Signed-off-by: Paweł Phan <szop.hektar_1w@icloud.com>
---
 inittab.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/inittab.c b/inittab.c
index 46ca796..f93ac68 100644
--- a/inittab.c
+++ b/inittab.c
@@ -126,7 +126,8 @@ static void child_exit(struct uloop_process *proc, int ret)
 	if (a->respawn < 0)
 		return;
 
-	if (!dev_exist(a->id)) {
+	/* A program with no terminal of its own has none to lose. */
+	if (a->id && *a->id && !dev_exist(a->id)) {
 		DEBUG(4, "Skipping respawn: device '%s' does not exist anymore\n", a->id);
 		return;
 	}
